            "review_title": "Review at Haveli Indian Restaurant-HCMC",
            "review_text": "Sam Dhillon\n3 contributions\n0\n2026; A New Year Lesson I’ll Never Forget – Apne Apne Hote Hain 🇮🇳❤️\nJan 2026 • Family\nOn 1st Jan in Ho Chi Minh City, I lost my passport, phone, and cash in a Grab taxi. With our flight the next day and two small kids, we were panicking. After hours of trying Grab and local help, nothing worked.\n\nAt the lowest moment, my wife noticed an Indian restaurant nearby. Though they were closing, the manager and chef from Uttarakhand, India stepped in like true heroes. They called the Punjabi owner, helped track the taxi driver, fed my hungry kids, and let us charge the phone.\n\nBy the time the kids finished eating, the driver arrived with his wife and returned the bag—everything safe 🙏\n\nThis wasn’t just help, it was family in\n a foreign land.\n\nProud to be an Indian. Apne apne hote hain 🇮🇳❤️\nRead more\nWritten January 1, 2026",
